      "message": "**Silent Memory Corruption on Small Files (`updater.cc`)** In `IsEcBinHasConfigPage`, the EOF stream checking logic is flawed, leading to uninitialized memory reads.\n\n```c\n// Current Code\nfile.read(reinterpret_cast\u003cchar*\u003e(\u0026config), sizeof(config));\nif (!file.good() \u0026\u0026 !file.eof()) { ... }\n\n```\n\nIf the file is smaller than `sizeof(config)`, `file.read` hits EOF. This sets both `failbit` and `eofbit`. `!file.good()` evaluates to `true`, but `!file.eof()` evaluates to `false`. The entire `if` block evaluates to `false`, and the application incorrectly proceeds to validate `config.code_valid_control_word` on uninitialized stack memory.\n\n* **Recommendation:** Check if the correct number of bytes were read.\n\n```c\nif (file.gcount() !\u003d sizeof(config)) {\n  FT_LOGE(\"Failed to read config page (file too small).\");\n  return std::unexpected(FtError::kResultFail);\n}\n\n```",
